---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Resume for Ted McCormick, DevOps Engineer and Software Developer"
			description="This is the resume page located on the personal/professional website for Edward C. 'Ted' McCormick, a software developer, DevOps Engineer, and Cloud Architect."
		/>
	</head>
	<body class="min-h-screen">
		<Header />
<main>
<div class="d-flex flex-column flex-md-row justify-content-between">
    <div class="m-1 p-3 text-center text-md-left">
        <h1 class="text-4xl text-blue-900">Take a look at what I've done.</h1>

        <p class="text-lg text-gray-400 ">These projects cover a lot of ground - both in content and technology used. Of course if you'd like to know more about any of them, <a class="text-blue-600 hover:underline" href="/contact">reach out and ask.</a></p>
    </div>


</div>
<div class="container mx-auto flex justify-between flex-col md:grid md:grid-cols-5 md:justify-content-center sm:px-4 md:auto-rows-fr md:gap-4">
<!--    <hr class="featurette-divider absolute">-->
<!--    <div class="flex flex-wrap my-4 justify-between featurette" id="adlister">-->



    <div class="md:col-span-3 p-4 m-4">
        <h2 class="featurette-heading">ted.mccormickhub.com (you're here!)<br>
            <span class="text-gray-700">Fast. Scalable. And Cloud Native. With integrated CI/CD and IAC</span></h2>
        <p class="text-xl font-light">I was a little rusty when I pulled this thing out of the depths of my GitHub repositorites, but over the course of a month or three (while also working full time and passing the AWS Cloud Developer Associate), I converted from Bootstrap to TailwindCSS, switched from jQuery to AlpineJS, re-engineered this into a cloud native/S3 bucket hosted app, and integrated an API Gateway with Lambda for 'contact me' functionality. <a class="text-blue-600 hover:underline" href="https://github.com/edwardmccormick/vanity-website/actions">And built a CI/CD pipeline in GitHub Actions, without any prior experience there.</a> Up next - blue/green deployments.</p>
        <div class="text-center"><a href="https://github.com/edwardmccormick/vanity-website" target="_blank"><button type="button" class="inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900 m-1">See the code</button></a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="md:col-span-2 m-4">
        <img src="/img/vanitysite.png" class="object-cover mx-auto" role="img" aria-label="A screenshot of a blog application" focusable="false">
    </div>

    <div class="md:col-span-2 m-4">
        <iframe class="aspect-[16/9] w-full mx-auto" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/6MERxOFnQOQ?si=YQp6H307Tsd0ITel" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe>
    </div>

    <div class="md:col-span-3 p-4 m-4">
        <h2 class="featurette-heading">Not Another Bookclub<br>
            <span class="text-gray-700">A very robust full stack application in Springboot, developed by a team as a capstone project for Codeup.</span></h2>
        <p class="text-xl font-light">Not Another Bookclub is, at its most basic, a social network built around a love of books and reading. NAB is a fully functional, end-to-end CRUD full-stack website, built with Java, SpringBoot, Thymeleaf, jQuery, Bootstrap, MySQL, Javascript, CSS, and HTML using Google APIs and internal RESTful endpoints.</p>
        <div class="text-center"><a href="https://github.com/Not-Another-Bookclub" target="_blank"><button type="button" class="inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900 m-1">See the code</button></a></div>
    </div>



    <div class="md:col-span-3 p-4 m-4">
        <h2 class="featurette-heading">Springboot Blog<br>
            <span class="text-gray-700"> A modern Java framework, serving a full stack modern CRUD application. </span></h2>
        <p class="text-xl font-light">This is a fully responsive, fully interactive, mobile responsive full stack application. It implements Spring Security and allows users to login and create blog posts, or edit their own blog posts, and for anyone to view a user's blog posts.</p>
        <div class="text-center"><a href="https://github.com/edwardmccormick/spring_blog" target="_blank"><button type="button" class="inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900 m-1">See the code</button></a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="md:col-span-2">
        <img src="/img/springboot_blog.png" class="object-cover mx-auto" role="img" aria-label="A screenshot of a blog application" focusable="false">

    </div>

    <div class="md:col-span-2 p-4 m-4">
        <img src="/img/Java_programming_language_logo.svg" class="object-cover mx-auto max-h-60"  role="img" aria-label="Java programming language logo">

    </div>
    <div class="md:col-span-3 p-4 m-4">
        <h2 class="featurette-heading">Adlister
            <br><span class="text-gray-700">A true full-stack CRUD application, in Java!</span></h2>
        <p class="text-xl font-light">Another pairs programming project, AdLister is a back end focused imitation of craigslist using Java, MySQL, servlets, and Tomcat to deploy the project. This is the first 'full-stack', true CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) application that I ever built. It uses a Java backend and (sort of minimal) styling, although I am quite proud of the form validation that we used.</p>
        <div class="text-center"><a href="https://github.com/edwardmccormick/java-adlister" target="_blank"><button type="button" class="inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900 m-1">See the code</button></a></div>
    </div>

<!--    </div>-->


<!--        <hr class="featurette-divider col-span-5">-->

<!--        <div class="flex flex-wrap my-4 justify-between featurette" id="weathermap">-->
            <div class="md:col-span-3 p-4 m-4">
                <h2 class="featurette-heading">Mapbox and Openweather.
                    <br><span class="text-gray-700">Two great APIs that taste better together.</span></h2>
                <p class="text-xl font-light">This is a fully responsive, fully interactive, mobile responsive Javascript app - it even has a hand-coded autocomplete function on the search bar. It uses jQuery, Bootstrap, AJAX, vanilla Javascript, and CSS and HTML.</p>
                <div class="text-center"><a href="https://github.com/edwardmccormick/codeup-web-exercises/blob/main/weather_map.html" target="_blank"><button type="button" class="inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900 m-1">See the code</button></a><a href="weather_map.html" target="_blank"><button type="button" class="m-1 inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900">See it live!</button></a></div>
            </div>
            <div class="md:col-span-2 p-4 m-4">
                <img src="/img/weathermap.png" class="object-cover mx-auto" width="500" height="500" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder: 500x500" focusable="false">

            </div>
<!--        </div>-->
<!--        <hr class="featurette-divider">-->
<!--        <div class="flex flex-wrap my-4 justify-between featurette" id="moviedatabase">-->
            <div class="md:col-span-2 p-4 m-4">
                <img src="/img/movie.png" class="object-cover mx-auto" role="img" id='' aria-label="Placeholder: 500x500" focusable="false">

            </div>
            <div class="md:col-span-3 p-4 m-4">
                <h2 class="featurette-heading">A media-front end, ready to integrate with a player.
                    <br><span class="text-gray-700">Mobile responsive, modern, and interactive. Just add movies!</span></h2>
                <p class="text-xl font-light">Another pairs programming project using multiple APIs to communicate with a private server and complete details of entries from a public server. </p>
                <div class="text-center"><a href="https://github.com/Joshua-and-Ted-Kalypso-Movie-Project/movie-database-pairs-programming" target="_blank"><button type="button" class="inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900 m-1">See the code</button></a><a href="movies.html"><button type="button" class="inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900 m-1" target="_blank">See it live!</button></a></div>
            </div>

<!--        </div>-->


<!--        <hr class="featurette-divider">-->

<!--        <div class="flex flex-wrap my-4 justify-between featurette" id="coffeeproject">-->
            <div class="md:col-span-3 p-4 m-4">
                <h2 class="featurette-heading">How about a nice hot cup of coffee?
                    <br><span class="text-gray-700">A responsive, interactive, Javascript web app.</span></h2>
                <p class="text-xl font-light">This is a pairs-programmed vanilla Javascript app that has a ton of functionality and even allows the user to add to the database and display. It's lovingly hand-coded with HTML, CSS, Bootstrap, and even touches a bit of LocalStorage and file permanence.</p>
                <div class="text-center"><a href="https://github.com/Jeremiah-and-Ted-Kalypso/coffee-project" target="_blank"><button type="button" class="inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900 m-1 ">See the code</button></a><a href="coffee.html" target="_blank"><button type="button" class="m-1 inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900">See it live!</button></a></div>
            </div>
            <div class="md:col-span-2 p-4 m-4">
                <img src="/img/coffeeproject.png" class="bd-placeholder-img bd-placeholder-img-lg featurette-image max-w-full h-auto mx-auto" focusable="false">

            </div>
<!--        </div>-->

<!--        <hr class="featurette-divider">-->

<!--        <div class="flex flex-wrap my-4 justify-between featurette" id="wireframe">-->

            <div class="md:col-span-2 p-4 m-4">
                <img src="/img/wireframe.png" class="bd-placeholder-img bd-placeholder-img-lg featurette-image max-w-full h-auto mx-auto" role="img" focusable="false">

            </div>
    <div class="md:col-span-3 p4 m-4">
        <h2 class="featurette-heading">And lastly, a beautiful, responsive home page mockup.
            <br><span class="text-gray-700">Built off wireframes, ready to be brought live.</span></h2>
        <p class="text-xl font-light">Another pairs programming project built with Bootstrap, CSS, and HTML. </p>
        <div class="text-center"><a href="https://github.com/Natalie-E-and-Ted-M/pairs-programming-bootstrap" target="_blank"><button type="button" class="inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900 m-1">See the code</button></a><a href="pairs-programming-bootstrap.html"><button type="button" class="inline-block align-middle text-center select-none border font-normal whitespace-no-wrap rounded py-1 px-3 leading-normal no-underline bg-gray-900 text-white hover:bg-gray-900 m-1" target="_blank">See it live!</button></a></div>
    </div>
<!--        </div>-->

<!--        <hr class="featurette-divider">-->

    </div>
    </div>
    </div>
</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
